<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67836" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μιλτ-όω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μίλτος</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cover with ruddle</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλίνθους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Supp.Epigr.</u>
					4.453.21
				</span></i>
			 (Didyma, <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχοινίον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					8.104
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖχον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>M.</u>
					10.126
				</span></i>
			; glossed by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλύνω</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			 or 
				Pass.
			, <i>cover oneself</i> or <i>be covered with
			ruddle</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.194
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεμιλτωμένῃ τῇ χειρί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
				</span></i>
			 l. c.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχοινίον
			μεμιλτωμένον</span> the rope <i>covered with ruddle</i> with
			which they drove loiterers out of the Agora to the Pnyx, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				22
			</span></i>, cf. Poll.l.c.</div>
